<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kermanshah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kermanshah is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the capital of Kermanshah province. It lies on the ancient route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a>, later called the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> Road. Nearby are the Behistun inscription of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> and the Sasanian rock reliefs of Taq-e Bostan. It is a centre of Kurdish population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kermanshah.jpg" alt="Kermanshah" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fars News Agency · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kermanshah_Photos_M6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
